  = must: preserve this decision as a deferral, not a rejection of mailbox IO, IRC, Matrix, web UI, LangGraph, Langflow, or future transport adapters
  = must: require a later explicit activation slice before adding package dependencies, lockfiles, imports from external adapter packages, mailbox readers, mailbox writers, read-cursor stores, filesystem watchers, socket listeners, IRC clients, Matrix clients, web servers, LangGraph adapters, Langflow exports, MCP clients, MCP servers, operations simulators, or runtime requirements
  = must: keep SOP, SJS, completion reviews, accepted decision documents, tracked fixture sources, expected ledgers, and canonical specifications as source authority
  = must: treat mailbox carrier records, adapter state, transport messages, graph checkpoints, Langflow flows, UI state, generated projections, generated reports, read cursors, dispatch attempts, and operations telemetry as carrier or execution projections until rewritten into accepted SOP authority by a later reviewed process

