  = must: require generated adapter and carrier outputs to remain ignored, disposable, and reproducible unless accepted by a later review
  = must: require adapter tests to prove carrier state, transport events, graph checkpoints, UI state, and mailbox read cursors cannot open gates or mutate source authority
  = must: require adapter tests to prove user or agent interactions route back to request records, SOP-first interrupts, human override records, conflict reviews, or completion reviews rather than direct mutation

& [AuthorityBoundaryAssessment: IR6CoordinationAdapters] is the authority fit assessment for future mailbox and transport surfaces
  + [fit_status] is future_adapter_candidates_preserved
  + [fit_reason] is mailbox IO, IRC, Matrix, web UI, LangGraph, and Langflow can become useful projections or execution surfaces after authority-preserving boundaries exist
  + [mismatch_status] is authority_boundary_mismatch_if_used_directly_as_truth
  + [mismatch_reason] is mailbox files, chat messages, adapter callbacks, UI events, graph checkpoints, Langflow flows, and process telemetry are carrier or execution surfaces rather than accepted SOP authority
  + [adapter_need] is map accepted LangSOP authority records into carrier inputs and map carrier outputs back into non-authoritative review requests until accepted by SOP review

  = must: prevent mailbox unread state, read cursor freshness, carrier delivery success, graph execution success, visual node state, UI click, chat command, or transport callback from satisfying readiness, completion review, source specification processing, or next-slice gates by itself
  = must: preserve human override and conflict review as reviewed SOP records rather than direct UI, transport, mailbox, or dispatch effects

